From b2cfd673828c2c649e2f9770a7ffd943d29f36f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:30:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 146/156] net: sparx5: leave a scheduler element alone that was
 never shaped
Organization: Wires

Deleting a tbf qdisc whose offload was refused, e.g. for a rate the
chip cannot represent, still reaches sparx5_tc_tbf_del().

The element is in no leak group, so sparx5_lg_get_group_by_index()
fails and leaves the group uninitialised, and the leak group update
that follows indexes the group table with it.

Skip the teardown when the element is in no leak group.

Fixes: e02a5ac6bf77 ("net: microchip: sparx5: add support for offloading tbf qdisc")
Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
index 5c172f281c7b..0d6c1a65d30d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
@@ -613,7 +613,8 @@ static int sparx5_shaper_del(struct sparx5_port *port, u32 layer, u32 idx)
 	struct sparx5_shaper sh = {0};
 	u32 group;
 
-	sparx5_lg_get_group_by_index(port->sparx5, layer, idx, &group);
+	if (sparx5_lg_get_group_by_index(port->sparx5, layer, idx, &group) < 0)
+		return 0;
 
 	return sparx5_shaper_conf_set(port, &sh, layer, idx, group);
 }
